NOTE: look for all the places that i note "MIDTERM CHANGE"

I pinpointed the cause of the great amount of thread wakeups to the fact that i am
using CV broadcast to wake up all R number of requesters during the steady state
every time i service one request. This is inefficient because i know exaclty which
thread that needs to wake up next, that being the next closest track. 
I thus single that thread out and wake it up. However once a thread has 
requested its last track, other tracks need to fill the spot since the servicer
might simply go back to sleep since the thread that woke up after having its last 
track serviced did not push anything on the quueue, thus do a special braodcast, see line
156. I made a map that will map requesters to their private CV, the servicer can
use this map to wake up the track returned by my "next" function, which returns 
the next closest track